461	\section{Proof of the soundness of the Pauli basis test}
462	
463	We can now prove the soundness theorem for the Pauli basis test, stated as Theorem~\ref{thm:pauli} in Chapter~\ref{chap:qpbt-test}.
464	
465	\begin{proof}
466		\proves{thm:pauli}
467		\uses{lem:qld-unitary, lem:qld-extraction-error-form, lem:pauli-completeness,
468			thm:naimark, lem:projective-strategy-setup, def:expanded-state,
469			def:EPR, def:povm-distance}
470		Let $(\ket{\psi},M)$ be a strategy for $\mathfrak{G}^{\mathrm{Pauli}}_{(q,m,d)}$ that succeeds with probability at least $1 - \eps$, where $\ket{\psi}$ is a bipartite state on registers $\mathrm{A}$ and $\mathrm{B}$. By Naimark's theorem (Theorem~\ref{thm:naimark}, as formulated in~\cite[Theorem 5.1]{Ji2020LowIndividualDegree}), at the cost of extending $\ket{\psi}$ by sufficiently many ancilla qubits initialized in the state $\ket{0}$, we may assume that the strategy is projective and that the state is padded as in the conventions of Lemma~\ref{lem:projective-strategy-setup} and the convention following it. Let $V_{\mathrm{A}}$ be the unitary acting on registers $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''$ given by Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary}, and let $\phi_{\mathrm{A}}$ be the isometry mapping register $\mathrm{A}$ to registers $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''$, where $\mathrm{A}'$ and $\mathrm{A}''$ are isomorphic to $(\C^q)^{\ot M}$, defined by
471		\[
472			\phi_{\mathrm{A}}\colon \ket{\theta}_{\mathrm{A}} \mapsto V_{\mathrm{A}} \bigl(\ket{\theta}_{\mathrm{A}} \ot (\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\ot M})_{\mathrm{A}' \mathrm{A}''}\bigr)\;;
473		\]
474		define $\phi_{\mathrm{B}}$ analogously.
475		% Reliance disclosure added: the proof chain of thm:pauli passes through
476		% lem:qld-4-7, whose source proof (lines 1277--1413 of
477		% 14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex) instantiates the classical low
478		% individual degree test at dimension 2m+2 without a divisibility
479		% hypothesis; the sentence below records the resulting outstanding
480		% obligation.
481		This invocation is where the analysis of the classical low individual degree
482		test enters. Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} rests on the polynomial-pair
483		measurement of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-7}, whose proof instantiates the
484		classical test in $2m+2$ variables and at present does so only when $2m+2$
485		divides $q$ --- a divisibility that fails for every admissible tuple with
486		$m \geq 2$. Three further steps of that same chain are likewise unproved.
487		The classical soundness statement invoked there,
488		Theorem~\ref{lem:ld-soundness},
489		is imported from Theorem~4.7 of~\cite{Ji2021Quantum} through an
490		identification of the game $\mathfrak{G}^{\mathrm{ld}}_{(q,m,d,1)}$ with
491		the two-prover tensor-code test for $\code^{\ot m}$, and neither that game
492		correspondence nor the bound on the auxiliary parameter of Theorem~4.7 under
493		which the stated error function $\delta_{\mathrm{ld}}$ is obtained has been
494		established. Both, with the divisibility obstruction, are documented in
495		\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility}. Furthermore, the combined-lines
496		consistency of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-13}, on which
497		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-7} relies, is established here only with the error
498		$m \cdot \poly(\eps, md/q)$, the error form $\poly(m^2 \eps, md/q)$
499		carried in its statement remaining unproved; the discrepancy and the
500		established form are documented in
501		\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}. The present proof is therefore
502		complete only modulo these four obligations. Since the
503		expanded state $\ket{\hat\psi}$ of Definition~\ref{def:expanded-state} is
504		exactly $\ket{\psi}$ with the halves of $M$ pairs
505		$\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}$ appended locally in registers
506		$\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''$ and $\mathrm{B}'\mathrm{B}''$, we have
507		$\phi_{\mathrm{A}} \ot \phi_{\mathrm{B}} \ket{\psi}
508		= V_{\mathrm{A}} \ot V_{\mathrm{B}} \ket{\hat\psi}$.
509		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} therefore yields a state $\ket{\mathrm{aux}}$
510		on registers $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'$ such that
511		\[
512			\bigl\| \phi_{\mathrm{A}} \ot \phi_{\mathrm{B}} \ket{\psi} - \ket{\mathrm{aux}} \ot \ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\ot M} \bigr\|^2 \leq \delta_{\mathrm{qld}}\;.
513		\]
514		% Transfer step added: the source (lines 1864--1875 of
515		% 14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex) passes directly from the
516		% conjugation estimates of lem:qld-unitary, which concern the
517		% unitarily conjugated operators V (M_h ot Id) V^dagger, to the
518		% corresponding estimates for the isometry phi, whose conjugation
519		% inserts the projection onto its range; the range-projection
520		% argument below supplies the missing step.
521		Item~2 of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} concerns the unitarily conjugated operators $N^W_h = V_{\mathrm{A}} \, (M^{(\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h)_{\mathrm{A}} \, V_{\mathrm{A}}^\dagger$, whereas conjugation by the isometry $\phi_{\mathrm{A}}$ additionally inserts the projection $Q_{\mathrm{A}} = \phi_{\mathrm{A}} \phi_{\mathrm{A}}^\dagger = V_{\mathrm{A}} \, \bigl(\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}\bra{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\ot M}\bigr)_{\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''} \, V_{\mathrm{A}}^\dagger$ onto the range of $\phi_{\mathrm{A}}$: since $(M^{(\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h)_{\mathrm{A}}$ and $\bigl(\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}\bra{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\ot M}\bigr)_{\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''}$ act on disjoint registers and hence commute,
522		\[
523			\phi_{\mathrm{A}} \, (M^{(\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h)_{\mathrm{A}} \, \phi_{\mathrm{A}}^\dagger
524			= V_{\mathrm{A}} \, \Bigl( (M^{(\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h)_{\mathrm{A}} \ot \bigl(\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}\bra{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\ot M}\bigr)_{\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''} \Bigr) \, V_{\mathrm{A}}^\dagger
